WEBVTT

00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:15,420
How often should I get a PET scan down?

00:00:15,420 --> 00:00:21,420
What's the best way to check for reoccurrence?

00:00:21,420 --> 00:00:27,420
Well, I think the best way to check for reoccurrence is probably a PET scan.

00:00:27,420 --> 00:00:36,420
And that would be the gold standard. The negative is that it's about two and a half times the radiation dose of a CT scan.

00:00:36,420 --> 00:00:42,420
And a lot of radiation from a PET scan. So you don't want to do it very often.

00:00:42,420 --> 00:00:49,420
It partly depends on the person I personally haven't had a scan down for.

00:00:49,420 --> 00:00:57,420
When two years ago that I did my scan, I think it was two years in March that I did my scan.

00:00:57,420 --> 00:01:02,420
And it was good except for some liver lesions.

00:01:02,420 --> 00:01:09,420
And am I going to do another scan? Probably not. So that's just me. So that's just my choice.

00:01:09,420 --> 00:01:13,420
So everybody's different. Everybody has different levels of anxiety.

00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:22,420
Everybody has different levels of what they're going to do from a standards of care approach because of our makeup, because of who we are.

00:01:22,420 --> 00:01:25,420
And because of our cancer with me.

00:01:25,420 --> 00:01:31,420
It's an easy decision for me because there is nothing with standards of care offers for my cancer.

00:01:31,420 --> 00:01:36,420
So I mean, statistically, I should have been dead a couple years ago.

00:01:37,420 --> 00:01:45,420
You know, statistically, it's a seven percent five years survival rate. You know, I've had six and a half years now, I think.

00:01:45,420 --> 00:01:58,420
So it's, it's, I'm not going to do another scan. You know, even if my symptoms get really bad, I'm from, I'm still not going to do a scan because nothing they can do for me.

00:01:58,420 --> 00:02:17,420
So, but you know, you have other options with breast cancer. So maybe you would do another scan. And you might have different levels of, you know, anxiety that you're struggling with with things to get another scan can be helpful to relieve that anxiety.

00:02:17,420 --> 00:02:40,420
So, you, is there damage that could occur because of the radiation of the scan? Sure. But you just got to weigh out what, you know, what's better for you emotionally to know that you're doing well or a deal with the radiation and detox that and support your body through that or to, to not.

00:02:40,420 --> 00:02:42,420
Everybody's got to weigh that out.

